      "worked": "The centre is $-\\frac{5}{3}$, so the common sum is three times the centre: $S=-5$. Opposite cells add to twice the centre, $-\\frac{10}{3}$. Thus the bottom-right cell is $-\\frac{10}{3}-(-3)=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and the top-right is $-\\frac{10}{3}-(-4)=\\frac{2}{3}$. Completing each row and column to $-5$ gives the square shown in the short answer.\n\nChecks:\n$$\\begin{aligned}-3-\\frac83+\\frac23&=-5\\\\2-\\frac53-\\frac{16}3&=-5\\\\-4-\\frac23-\\frac13&=-5.\\end{aligned}$$\nEvery column and both diagonals also sum to $-5$.",
